      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Auto-declining friend requests is not meant to prevent viewer spam, but instead it is intended to prevent some attack cases we've seen in usage.\nWe could except people in the same instance as you, but that kinda opens up some surface I don't think we're OK with opening up. \nThe intent was that you could still send a friend request to others when this mode is on, so its sort of a soft version of the Discord privacy options for friend requests (which might be something we eventually do). Thoughts?",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "60567397e93e7c49c4b52c6c",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5d6ac3d319a45a329c545086",
        "alias": "Governing Marmot",
        "aliasID": "65c287d2ed6eefce4c73736f",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/f73d4b48b1338d88c25009c07995e25b.png",
        "created": "2019-08-31T19:00:35.115Z",
        "name": "Sasha Mason",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5b0746088fa72313783e3269",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2021-03-20T22:13:43.171Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 2,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "605671d5e3c42a495db614c1",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 8
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Agreed. Otherwise it would just be more difficult to add people when I'm out exploring and socializing. It would still protect streamers who are in their own private instance, but wouldn't make it more difficult to add someone that I am hanging out with right now. Also, if there were two people in streamer mode, neither of them would be able to add each other without first disabling it, which wouldn't be ideal at all. Keep in mind that most people will not (or cannot due to being mute / different language) ask if they can add someone when they meet them ingame. Unless I'd be able to tell that I cannot add them right now, I also wouldn't be able to approach them and ask if they would be fine with it or not.\nAlso why it being a separate setting altogether would be better as to not make streamers more of a target if anyone can have it (Would also prevent friend request spam for world and avatar creators)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "605674cb3643f440d418918f",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5d6ac3d319a45a329c545086",
        "alias": "Governing Marmot",
        "aliasID": "65c287d2ed6eefce4c73736f",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/f73d4b48b1338d88c25009c07995e25b.png",
        "created": "2019-08-31T19:00:35.115Z",
        "name": "Sasha Mason",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
