          "aliasID": "65ba088fed6eefce4ca8dc62",
          "anonymized": false,
          "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/a96149971e91f0ceb638e9e86cef2b08.gif",
          "created": "2018-04-09T03:11:40.225Z",
          "name": "Tupper - VRChat Head of Community",
          "serviceAccount": false,
          "urlName": null
        }
      ],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": "6056729900eea75d8465dc80",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "605671d5e3c42a495db614c1",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 12
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: The problem is that two people in streamer mode wouldn't be able to add each other at all, as well as making it more difficult for people who are just hanging out to add people because they wouldn't know if that person is using streamer mode or not (and there are a lot of streamers in VRChat). Discord would at least notify me that I am not able to add someone, VRChat doesn't do that. And not every streamer would have an issue with friend requests from people in the room, so the lack of customizability in that regard also makes it not ideal. If two people in streamer mode would be able to add each other, it would be bypassable and defeat the original intention.\nThat's why I think having a separate setting for when you can and cannot be added (similar to Discord) would be the better solution. It would be separate from streamer mode (which Discord has as well) in case you do want friend requests, you would be able to prevent random friend requests from people you have never met regardless of the mode or block it out completely if you absolutely never want anyone to add you. Most importantly, Discord actually does let you know about this. I would hate trying to add someone only for that request to go into the void and me not knowing about it, so I'm not even able to ask  them if they can add me instead to see if they would be okay with it or not.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
